Chapter 10: Discussion of Alternative Solution Approaches

The choice of CPW-MCTS with Lagrangian relaxation merits justification against viable alternatives.

· Constrained Policy Optimization (CPO): assumes fixed action space and differentiable policies; incompatible with discrete graph-structured actions.
· Approximate Dynamic Programming (ADP): requires tractable value function approximation over hybrid state space, still an open problem.
· Exhaustive Search: feasible for 12 nodes (4096 states) under nominal conditions (Baseline E), but intractable with stochastic fault injection.
· Model Predictive Control (MPC): structurally similar but lacks deep exploration and formal regret guarantees; included as Baseline F.
· CPW-MCTS advantages: handles non-stationary action spaces, finite-sample regret bounds, natural constraint integration via Lagrange multipliers, domain-informed priors, anytime operation.

